THOUGHT: The FloatBuffer overload should mirror the null-check behavior of the float[] overload to satisfy NullAway, since instances is nullable. I’ll update the method to check instances for null and throw the same exception if it’s not set, then later we can re-run the build. For now, I’ll modify Mesh.java accordingly.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '366,369c\  public Mesh updateInstanceData(
      int targetOffset, FloatBuffer source, int sourceOffset, int count) {
    if (instances != null) {
      this.instances.updateInstanceData(targetOffset, source, sourceOffset, count);
    } else {
      throw new GdxRuntimeException(
          "An InstanceBufferObject must be set before updating instance data!");
    }
    return this;
  }' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/graphics/Mesh.java
```

